Minato's patch 0027 to ANGLE (BSD-3-Clause), on top of 0025: no GL call parks its thread in the background.

Why: iOS refuses GPU commits in the background. Patch 0025 keeps the command buffers of a background commit in a FIFO
for the foreground, but a call that wanted a result of that work (glFinish, a readback, a CPU access to a resource the
work uses, a client wait, a query's result) or a commit that found the FIFO full still waited for the foreground,
parking the app's thread there. On Android the GPU runs in the background, so each of those calls returns. A thread
parked inside a GL call holds the app's own locks with it (a Ren'Py game's: the GIL and SDL's audio lock, with
Android's onStop waiting 8 s for it).

What: in the background (the embedder's commit gate holds commits back):
- CommandBuffer::wait(WaitUntilFinished), glFinish's and a readback's wait, returns without the result;
- CommandQueue::waitUntilSerialCompleted answers a wait for a deferred command buffer, of any length, as done;
- CommandQueue::ensureResourceReadyForCPU returns at once for a resource the deferred work uses: the CPU reads or
  writes it as it has it (a readback has the pixels from before the deferred work);
- a full FIFO (32 command buffers or 128 MiB) commits its oldest command buffer instead of a wait: iOS refuses that
  commit (an error of the command buffer, not fatal), its work is lost, as a dropped frame's is, and ANGLE's
  bookkeeping completes it;
- each wait that went on without its result is counted (ANGLEMetalDeferredSkipped; the park line's dskip=).
In the foreground every wait first commits the FIFO, and a thread of ANGLE's own (never an app's) waits for the
foreground while command buffers are deferred and then commits every queue's FIFO, so that work deferred by a thread
with nothing more to commit runs at the foreground too.

